{
  "_comment": "Fixed relevance benchmark for the search layer, reusable across sessions. `must` is a list of concept regexes tested against title+prose; ALL must match for a result to count as relevant. Conjunctive on purpose: an earlier version used a single permissive alternation and scored 100% on everything, because BM25 only returns documents containing the query terms in the first place, making 'mentions any query word' a tautology. Each concept accepts synonyms so any reasonable reading of the query counts.",
